   "id": "ac-voltage",
   "kind": "definition",
   "section": "20.5",
   "name": "AC voltage, $\\kV = \\kVo\\sin 2\\pi \\kf\\kt$",
   "statement": "An AC voltage is a voltage that fluctuates sinusoidally with time, $V = V_0\\sin 2\\pi ft$, where $V_0$ is its peak value and $f$ its frequency.",
   "introduces": "alternating-current",
   "prereqs": [
