   "id": "rms-current",
   "kind": "definition",
   "section": "20.5",
   "name": "RMS current, $\\kIrms = \\kIocur/\\sqrt{2}$",
   "statement": "The rms current is the root mean square of an alternating current, $I_\\text{rms} = I_0/\\sqrt{2}$, where $I_0$ is the peak current.",
   "introduces": "rms-values",
